Block: particle_gibbs_block
Version: 0.1.0
Title: Particle Gibbs (conditional SMC / PGAS) sampler for continuous latent
 state-space paths
Description: Samples the continuous latent state path x_{1:T} of a univariate
 first-order state-space model x_1 ~ m(.), x_t | x_{t-1} ~ f(.|x_{t-1}),
 y_t | x_t ~ g(.|x_t), where the transition f or emission g is nonlinear or
 non-Gaussian and admits no closed-form (Kalman/FFBS) conditional. Model
 structure is supplied through four callbacks (initial draw, transition draw,
 emission log-weight, transition log-density); the dynamics parameters theta and
 the observations are read from the block_context each sweep and are sampled by
 sibling blocks. Sampling uses conditional sequential Monte Carlo (Particle
 Gibbs) with a bootstrap proposal and optional ancestor sampling (PGAS), which
 leaves the latent-path full conditional invariant for any particle count
 N >= 2. The stochastic-volatility log-volatility path is the worked example.
Author: Alex Ziyu Jiang
Maintainer: Alex Ziyu Jiang
License: GPL-3.0-or-later
EngineKind: mcmc
ConstraintKinds: none
RoutingKey: continuous latent state-space path (nonlinear/non-Gaussian SSM)
SelectWhen: univariate continuous latent state-space path with a nonlinear /
 non-Gaussian transition or emission (no closed-form smoother)
Skill: skills/particle_gibbs_block.md
Tests: test_particle_gibbs_block.cpp
Depends: core (>= 1.0)
Example: examples/StochasticVolatility.cpp
ValidationSkill: skills/particle_gibbs_block_validation.md
ChecksApplicable: BL1, BL2 (core #1-#26: none triggered by mechanism --
 gradient-free, fixed-dim, no constraint transform)
KernelTier: none
